{
  "case_version": 1,
  "name": "leak-window-between-versions",
  "description": "Two finally-legal egress versions at px-b. v1 sends generation-1 markers to svc-orders, which accepts (t-alpha, L1). v2 sends generation-2 markers to svc-next with label L2, which accepts (t-alpha, L2); it also keeps a gen-1 compatibility rule so markers already in flight are not stranded, but that rule preserves label L1 while the link now points at svc-next. Switching before the drain therefore hands an in-flight gen-1 marker to svc-next as (t-alpha, L1) -- a pair svc-next does not accept, i.e. a tenant-isolation leak. Draining gen 1 with a barrier before the switch removes the window.",
